.TH ZEC\-SAPLING 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.1.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
zec\-sapling \- zec\-sapling [\-\-count N] [\-\-unified] [\-\-viewkey\-out FILE] < BIP39 mnemonic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
{"error":"bad_mnemonic"}
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\-\-unified also emits, per account, the ZIP\-316 unified address (orchard + sapling + p2pkh, all
at the account's first valid Sapling diversifier index j, as zcashd/librustzcash do) and the
transparent t1 address at m/44'/133'/i'/0/j. Orchard keys: ZIP\-32 m/32'/133'/i' (orchard crate).
Zcash Sapling (ZIP\-32): seed = BIP39(mnemonic, ""), account i = m/32'/133'/i', default
(first valid diversifier) payment address, encoded bech32 "zs". stdout: PUBLIC rows only.
\-\-viewkey\-out writes the accounts' extended full viewing keys (bech32 "zxviews", secret:
they reveal all incoming and outgoing funds, but cannot spend) to FILE, new, mode 0600.
The spending key is never output.
.SH OPTIONS
See SYNOPSIS; this tool has no separate long\-option list beyond \-\-help.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
(first valid diversifier) payment address, encoded bech32 "zs". stdout: PUBLIC rows only.
\-\-viewkey\-out writes the accounts' extended full viewing keys (bech32 "zxviews", secret:
The spending key is never output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success (JSON lines may still carry status fields such as done / no_candidates).
.TP
2
Bad input, unsupported shape, or tool\-reported failure (JSON status is the detail).
.TP
3
Refused on purpose (watch\-only, policy deny, human abort, missing confirmation).
.PP
Other nonzero codes are tool\-specific; always read the last JSON status line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
See recipes/ for end\-to\-end flows. Search for zec\-sapling in recipes/*.md.
\&./blocktools run zec\-sapling \-\-count 1 \-\-viewkey\-out /out/zec.view < /in/mnemonic.txt
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: audit before use with real funds. See docs/SECURITY.md.
Run secret\-touching tools only inside ./blocktools run (sealed, offline).
